# Review: TasksPlugin (Outline and Journal)

The spec covers only the outline and journal half of plugin-tasks; the package has since grown a
task, task-set, milestone and remote-session model the spec does not mention. Of what it does
cover, the outline editor is solid (CRDT text, the shared `outliner` extension with Tab indent,
hashtags, a Delete row menu), and quick journal entry is well tested by `quick-entry.test.ts` and
`Journal.test.ts`. The journal view diverges: entries render oldest first with today at the
bottom, and selecting a calendar date does nothing to the list. There is no `createOutline`
operation; outlines are made through the generic create-object entry.

Of 36 items (34 verdicts: the spec reuses the ids `Journal` and `Outline` for a type and a component, so one verdict covers each pair): 11 done, 12 untested, 3 partial, 1 diverged, 7 missing. Findings:

- **F-2.3 diverged.** `Journal` sorts entry keys ascending and autofocuses the last (today), so the
  list is oldest-to-newest, not newest-to-oldest.
- **F-3.2 missing.** `JournalArticle` passes no select handler to `Calendar`; only the reverse
  direction (entry date button → calendar scroll) is wired.
- **createOutline missing.** No such operation exists; the Outline create-object entry in
  `create-object.ts` covers the navtree path, and T-1 is not automated.

